Task: Pointer invariance regression guard
Phase: 2 (Input Modality & Timing Compliance)
Scope: packages/core/tests/pointerInvariance.test.ts

10 specs, all passing on first run - expected for a regression guard, which
asserts an existing invariant rather than driving new behaviour.

Covers: engagement tolerance, out-of-tolerance reset, unlock on release after
full traversal, onTurn during pointer traversal, segmented checkpoint on
release, mid-segment snapback to last checkpoint, inactivity timer arming under
pointer, and no timer when checkpointTimeoutMs is unset.

The load-bearing one is modality: a pointer-only gesture must never report
keyboard, because that is exactly the condition under which the inactivity
timeout is suppressed. A leak from the stepping path into pointer traversal
would silently disable the timeout that segmented mode exists to provide, with
no other test failing.

Full suite 383 passed, 5 failed - only the Phase 0 baseline specs.
